I wrote the plan for two tasks in session_plan/ (task_01.md, task_02.md, issue_responses.md), but nothing is committed. git add refused because session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the plan commit did nothing. The files exist on disk for the implementation phase to read.

Task 1 (product): Fixes #1144 item 2, Part of #1121. Remove yoyo's own copies of Claude limits and read them from yoagent 0.27.2's table instead. The two copies are the Claude branch of model_context_window_table in commands_info.rs (it still says sonnet-4-5 has a 1M window, against 200K) and anthropic_output_maximum in agent_builder.rs.
• It starts by printing yoyo's values and yoagent's side by side for every Claude id yoyo offers.
• A test then requires the two to match, with near-miss rows for an unknown id and for sonnet-4-5.
• The last step runs the built binary from /tmp on Bedrock anthropic.claude-opus-4-7. If the guessed-limits warning is gone, that closes #1121's last row; if not, the output goes on the ticket.
• If any copied limit is left, the title drops to "Part of #1144".

Task 2 (product): Part of #1147. I filed #1147 while planning. It takes the non-Claude list census out of a #1144 comment, where it had no ticket of its own.
• The task checks five ids that look made-up against yoagent and the vendors' own model pages, with a URL for each: o4-mini-high, mixtral-8x7b-32768, grok-2, gpt-5.5-mini, MiniMax-M1-40k.
• Any id that doesn't exist or is retired comes off the lists. A test pins that the dropped ids aren't offered and still get the "Unknown model" line.
• If a vendor page can't be reached, the result is "could not check" and the id stays.
• If one of them turns out to be a provider's default, it is left alone and noted on #1147.

